  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LEARN to Read</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Nigeria):  With FY 2022 funds this activity will: .Improve reading outcomes for pupils in grades 1-3 in select Nigerian states; .Strengthen the capacity of the Nigerian basic education system to expand and replicate evidence-based reading practices that promote quality teaching and learning, especially for girls and those from disadvantaged groups; and.Provide students with the foundational skills and abilities to progress to higher levels of education and become self-reliant citizens..In FY 2022, LEARN to Read partnered with federal, state, and local education officials to improve pre-service and in-service teacher capacity, and develop policies that strengthen the enabling environment for sustainable education reforms.This activity includes a small grants component to engage youth, especially young girls, in education development in their communities..LEARN to Read activity focus is on foundational learning including reading skills of pupils, especially girls, in grades 1 and 2 in the conflict affected northern states of Bauchi, Sokoto and Adamawa.   A rapid gender assessment was conducted and the evaluation will include disaggregation of all people level indicators by sex and age cohort at minimum. In 2022, gender and inclusion training was conducted for LEARN staff. The activity partners with other states to  access services and technical assistance to deliver evidence-based reading instruction in the early grades. ..... ...</narrative>
  </description>
